      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Situated among oak‑studded hills between Woodside, Redwood City, and San Carlos, Emerald Lake Hills is bounded by Edgewood Road, Alameda de las Pulgas, Farm Hill Boulevard, and I‑280.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerald_Lake_Hills%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Upper Emerald Lake is privately held by shoreline owners, while Lower Emerald Lake is owned and operated by the Emerald Lake Country Club.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerald_Lake_Hills%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
